Description:
    Copy the agent skills crosswire ships into this app's .claude/skills/, so coding
    agents (Claude Code and compatible) pick them up when working in this app.

    The shipped set is discovered from the gem at run time; today it is:

      crosswire-ui          Using the primitives: Rule 0 before any JavaScript, the
                            cw builder's three usage levels, and the survivability
                            tier (preserve, loading/fallback, authorized streams).

      crosswire-composing   Composite widgets (modal, dropdown, drawer, toast, …):
                            decompose into shipped primitives and stack their attrs —
                            no new controller.

      crosswire-authoring   Writing a NEW Stimulus controller: whether it should be a
                            controller at all, the component shape, the R-rules, and
                            the sharp edges that bite first-time controllers.

    Idempotent: an unchanged file is a silent no-op, and a locally edited copy is
    never overwritten without --force. Re-run after upgrading the gem to refresh the
    skills.

Example:
    rails generate crosswire:skills

        Copies every shipped skill into .claude/skills/<name>/.

    rails generate crosswire:skills --force

        Refreshes the skills, overwriting locally edited copies.
